<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108880" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόξηρ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>somewhat dry,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτύσματα, γλῶσσα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Coac.</u>
				363
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epid.</u>
				7.22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τοῖς ὑ.</span> in <i>dry
				places,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.915e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>lean, slender,</i> of parts that have not much flesh over them,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				4
			</span></i> vulg. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ξυρα</span> codd. opt.), 
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόξυροι</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Art.</u>
				77
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
